00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:21.660
Now something that I did
actually learn on my own

00:15:21.660 --> 00:15:26.020
is that validations can exist
externally and internally.

00:15:26.020 --> 00:15:30.300
So in my case, or in my
opinion, the best scenario

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:33.780
has always been that validations
are implemented externally,

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:37.150
whether that's at the point of
data collection or whatever.

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:40.290
If it's external, if it's
externally implemented,

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:43.740
it might increase the chances
of your data being actually like

00:15:43.740 --> 00:15:46.750
workable and clean by the time
it gets to you internally.

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:50.010
Hopefully it's less work,
but my usual scenario

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:51.960
has been that there's
no validation done

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:53.800
and that I have
to do everything.

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:56.520
